{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion` type implements\n`trust_but_verify::graph::Criterion<D>` for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    type Ok: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> NodeId<D>;\n    fn criterion_path(&self) -> CriterionPath;\n    fn version(&self) -> CriterionVersion;\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        ctx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject fixes the shape of the trait `Criterion<D>`:\n- It has a `Send + Sized` supertrait.\n- `Ok` is bound by `Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send`.\n- It has the methods `source_node_id`, `criterion_path` and `version`.\n- `execute` takes `self` and `&mut ValidationContext<'_, D>`, and returns a `Send` future of `Result<Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>`.\n\nThis is a structural, compile-time contract. The marked tests check it by implementing and using the trait.\n\n**Tests that implement and call the trait**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` uses `Review<O>`, which implements `Criterion<Application>` for a generic `O`.\n  - Its `source_node_id`, `criterion_path` and `version` are called and asserted. It asserts source node `Node(1)`, path `[\"behavior\"]` and version `\"v1\"`.\n  - `execute` runs via `verify`, and its output is asserted.\n  - The `Ok` values are serialized to `{\"satisfied\":false,\"details\":[...]}` and `null`, and reloaded as typed outputs. This covers the `Serialize` and `DeserializeOwned` bounds.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]` implements and runs a second domain (`Memory`) with its own `Review`. It asserts the version and the stored output.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` runs a deterministic criterion for a third domain whose `execute` uses `ValidationContext`. `NoAgentConfigured` is returned when `ask` is called without an agent.\n\n**Tests of the `Send` requirements**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync]` wraps the `verify`, `store_evidence`, `load_evidence` and `refresh_evidence` futures in `send(...)`, which requires `T: Send`.\n  - It uses `Cell<u32>` as `Ok`, which is `Send` but not `Sync`.\n  - It also uses a `Review` carrying a `Cell` counter. This shows the trait does not require `Sync` for `Ok` or for the criterion, and that the execution futures are `Send`.\n\n**Other tests and gaps**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks that `Criterion` is exported at its documented path and kind. It also checks that the shipping Habeas consumer compiles against the SDK.\n- No obligation in the text is left untested. Implementing the trait for several domains, with differing `Ok` types, compiles only if the declared member signatures match.\n- I found no behavior in the text that a reasonable violation would pass past these tests.",
  "references": "a879f0ae49401bc00fac45ea5398c96091e5d5707b6490f80c3427a3894f1a04",
